1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,100
What happens when you change

2
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:01,860
just one byte?

3
00:00:02,367 --> 00:00:03,687
Here are two tiny files.

4
00:00:04,187 --> 00:00:05,467
One contains the letter A.

5
00:00:05,887 --> 00:00:07,127
The other contains the letter

6
00:00:07,127 --> 00:00:07,407
B.

7
00:00:07,733 --> 00:00:08,873
Compute a hash for each

8
00:00:08,873 --> 00:00:10,773
file. Even this small change

9
00:00:10,773 --> 00:00:12,233
gives us two different fingerprints.

10
00:00:12,767 --> 00:00:13,907
Compare the result with a

11
00:00:13,907 --> 00:00:15,867
trusted hash. A match helps

12
00:00:15,867 --> 00:00:17,427
check integrity, but it does

13
00:00:17,427 --> 00:00:18,547
not prove the file is

14
00:00:18,547 --> 00:00:18,827
safe.
